-- title:
--   Vertical unit on the blown-up supersingular chart adapted to an end
-- statement:
--   **Arithmetic data.** Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and let $\ell\ge 3$ be a prime with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` requires a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$, and let `hK` identify $K$ with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q * ℓ) ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q * ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of level $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ attached to the subgroup $H=$ `levelH (q * ℓ) M'`, which is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, that is, the group of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain which is henselian local with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $A$-algebra structure on $L$ for which $L$ is the fraction field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (`hξA`), and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise base change to $L$ of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}\cdot(\text{integral power series})$ of the modular $j$-function. Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$, and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A ↥K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$, and write $X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A ↥K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) for the integral model obtained as the pushout glueing $\operatorname{Spec}C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $j^{-1}$-chart algebra along the middle algebra, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ and chart immersion `ιFin` from $\operatorname{Spec}C$.
--
--   **The supersingular point.** Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $C$ containing the image of $\varpi$, supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $j_0\in\Omega$ such that every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j_0$ has no nonzero $\Omega$-rational point killed by $q$.
--
--   **The rigidification hypothesis `hArig`.** This hypothesis asserts, for every point $z$ of $X$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of the image of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec}C$ with `ιFin` image $z$ satisfying the same supersingularity condition as in `hss`, the existence of: a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f$ congruent to the Drinfeld form `drinfeldForm q W` $=X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e:\ \widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}\ \xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\ S:=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))\,v-f\,u\bigr),$$
--   where the completion is the adic completion of the stalk at its maximal ideal, subject to seven clauses, stated there in full and summarised here: (a) $e$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to the constant $C(\sigma a)$; (b) the chart algebra $C$ is stable under every automorphism $\tau$ of $K/L$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ` (for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on [`CohCarrier.GammaH N₀ H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g\ne0$, all $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the base change of $p_f/p_g$, and all $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ under $\iota$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\!$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹` equals that of $f\mid_k\!$`conjElemN (q*ℓ) γ⁻¹`); (c) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ the restriction of such a $\tau$ to $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$; (d) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and such a $\tau$ whose restriction to $C$ is the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in\mathrm{Mat}_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ is compatible, through $e$ and the canonical map from $C$ to the completed stalk, with the restriction of $\tau$, fixes all constants, satisfies $\theta(X_{j})\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0,X_1$, and satisfies $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M_{ij}\equiv c\cdot\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, together with $c\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$ and $c\not\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; (e) two primes of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$, neither containing both images of $X_0,X_1$, each containing a form $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h_i$ with $h_i\in(X_0,X_1)^2$ and with $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; (f) for a prime $P$ of $S$ over $\sigma\varpi$ containing a form $X_0+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$ and not containing both images of $X_0,X_1$, an element $a\in C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (g) the series `jqNModC L (q*ℓ)` lies in $K$ and in $C$, differs from some $a_0\in A$ by an element of $y'$, and this difference is carried by $e$ to the class of some $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ with $e_0\ge1$ whose leading $e_0$-form evaluates to a unit at every pair $a,b\in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   **The chosen point and presentation.** Let $z$, $\varpi_z$ (`hϖz`, `hz`), and $y'$ (`hy'`, `hss'`) be such a point and chart point, with `hy'y` requiring $y'$ to correspond to $y$. Let $W_1$, $\sigma_1$ (with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$), $f_1,u_1,v_1$ (units $u_1,v_1$; $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$) and $e_1$ be data as above, and let $S$ denote $W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1)$, with `mkS` the quotient map and `germY` the canonical homomorphism from $C$ to the stalk at $z$. The hypothesis `hW₁` asserts that these data satisfy exactly the seven clauses (a)–(g) described above, with $W_1,\sigma_1,e_1,S$ in place of $W,\sigma,e,S$.
--
--   **The centre, the $\varpi_t$-chart and the special valuation ring.** Let $J$ be an ideal of $C$ and let `hJ` require $J$ to be the infimum of the set of ideals of the form
--   $$\mathrm{comap}_{\tau|_C}\Bigl(\mathrm{comap}_{e_1\circ\,\text{(completion)}\circ\text{germY}}\bigl(\,\mathrm{mkS}(C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)),\ \mathrm{mkS}(X_0),\ \mathrm{mkS}(X_1)\,\bigr)\Bigr),$$
--   where $\gamma$ ranges over $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ over the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. Let $B$ be an $A$-subalgebra of $K$ with `hB`: $B$ is the subalgebra generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\exists\,i\in J,\ x\varpi_t=i\}$, i.e. $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   The hypothesis `hR1` requires $C\subseteq B$ and that every element of $K$ be a quotient of two elements of $B$ with nonzero denominator. The hypothesis `hR2` requires $B$ to be formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$, with $B/(\varpi)$ of Krull dimension at most $1$. The hypothesis `hR3` (five clauses) requires: an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$; and $f\in K$ lies in $W$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hEQ` (five clauses) requires: (1) for every $\mathrm{GF}(q^2)$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$, a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables over $k$ by `drinfeldPoly q k − 1`) whose kernel consists of the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, which is compatible with $A\to k\to$ `CoordRing`, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$ there is $c\in\mathrm{GF}(q^2)^\times$ with $(\,$`redQ q γ`$,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(\bar\gamma,c)\mapsto\det(\bar\gamma)\,c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho\circ\tau=$ `hAction q k` of that element composed with $\rho$, and $c\ne1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; (2) $B$ is stable under the level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; (3) every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is the image, under some level automorphism attached to some $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, of the set of elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$; (4) an element of $B$ all of whose images under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; (5) a level automorphism attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $y$ on $C$ preserves $W$.
--
--   **The end.** Let $O$ be a subring of $K$ and let `hO` require the existence of a nonzero $a\in J$, of a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a:=C[J/a]$ (the subalgebra generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\exists\,i\in J,\ xa=i\}$, viewed over $A$), such that $O$ is the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (that is, $f\in O$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$, $h\notin P$), such that no element of $y$ becomes a unit of $O$, and such that $B\not\subseteq O$. Further, `hOW` requires $O\subseteq W$, `hOloc` that $O$ be local, `hOnoe` that $O$ be noetherian, and `hCO` that $C\subseteq O$.
--
--   Finally, `hIgStab` requires that every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that an element of $L$ lies in $V$ exactly when it comes from $A$, the image of $\varpi$ lies in $\mathfrak m_V$, $C\subseteq V$, and some $c\in C$ has the property that $p(c)\in V$ and is a unit of $V$ for every monic $p\in A[T]$, is preserved by every level automorphism attached to $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exist an integer $n\ge1$ and an element $s\in J^n$, nonzero in $K$, such that the following four assertions hold.
--
--   1.
--
--   $s\cdot(\varpi_t^{\,n})^{-1}\in B$ and $\varpi_t^{\,n}\cdot s^{-1}\in B$.
--
--   2.
--
--   For every nonzero $a\in J$ and every maximal ideal $P$ of $C[J/a]$ such that $O$ is the localisation of $C[J/a]$ at $P$ (that is, $f\in O$ iff $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in C[J/a]$ and $h\notin P$), one has $s\cdot(a^n)^{-1}\in O$ and $a^n\cdot s^{-1}\in O$.
--
--   3.
--
--   For every valuation subring $V$ of $K$ such that an element of $L$ lies in $V$ exactly when it comes from $A$, and such that the image of $\varpi$, if it lies in $V$, lies in $\mathfrak m_V$: if $j\in V$, if $p(j)$ is a unit of $V$ whenever $p\in A[T]$ is monic and $p(j)\in V$, and if some element of $O$ lies outside $V$, then there is $c\in J^n$ with $c\cdot s^{-1}\notin V$.
--
--   4.
--
--   For every $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ in the above sense, $\tau(s)=s$.
--
--   This is the existence of a vertical unit on the blow-up of the $j$-finite chart along the weighted centre $J$ at a supersingular point: an element $s\in J^n$ which trivialises $J^n$ both on the $\varpi_t$-chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$ and at the prescribed end $O$, which fails to be a generator at the remaining Igusa-type valuations, and which is invariant under the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_subalgebra_le_blowupChart_inf_end_finiteType_isLocalization_of_end_blowupChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_subalgebra_le_blowupChart_inf_end_finiteType_isLocalization_of_end_blowupChart), where $C[J^n/s]$ serves as an affine finite-type neighbourhood of the end stable under those automorphisms and having $O$ as a localisation.
-- source:
